From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: accept the association link in M2 of a rekeying

IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 12.7.6.3 has message 2 of a rekeying carry an
MLO Link KDE for each setup link. wpa_auth_validate_ml_kdes_m2()
refused a KDE for the association link of the authenticator in every
message 2 and ended the association with reason 2.

wpa_supplicant leaves out only its own association link. Once the AP
MLD moved the association to another link, after a Link
Reconfiguration that deletes the association link
(hostapd_link_reconf_resp_tx_status()), the KDE of the new association
link was refused, and the first PTK rekey disconnected the non-AP MLD.
836-AP-MLD-keep-the-association-of-a-non-AP-MLD-at-a-lin.patch
moves the association in the same way at an AP removal of the link.

In message 2 of a rekeying (a pairwise key is installed), accept the
KDE of the association link where it names the address of that link,
and do not count it among the affiliated links. In message 2 of the
initial 4-way handshake, the KDE of the association link is still
refused.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
@@ -3828,6 +3828,14 @@ static int wpa_auth_validate_ml_kdes_m2(
 			n_links++;
 			continue;
 		}
+
+		/* M2 of a rekeying names each setup link, the association link
+		 * included (IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 12.7.6.3) */
+		if (i == sm->mld_assoc_link_id && sm->pairwise_set &&
+		    ether_addr_equal(sm->mld_links[i].peer_addr,
+				     kde->mlo_link[i] + 1))
+			continue;
+
 		if (!sm->mld_links[i].valid || i == sm->mld_assoc_link_id) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 				   "RSN: MLD: Invalid link ID=%u", i);
